lines=['# Microeconomics wording and graph-assessment audit','', 'Date: October 3, 2026. Status: **read-only audit; no cleanup performed.**','', '| Scope / finding | Count |','|---|---:|',f'| Total Micro questions screened | {len(r):,} |',f'| Graph/image-bearing questions reviewed | {metrics["graph_image_questions_reviewed"]:,} |',f'| Distinct image contents visually inspected | {metrics["distinct_image_contents_visually_inspected"]} (233 referenced files) |',f'| Wording finding groups | {len(w)} |',f'| Distinct wording-affected records | {len(wi)} |',f'| Directly optional graph questions | {metrics["directly_optional_graph_questions"]} |',f'| Graph-choice shortcut questions | {metrics["graph_choice_shortcut_questions"]} |',f'| Unique affected records across all categories | {len(affected)} |','',f'The two graph categories are mutually exclusive. {len(wi&gi)} records have both wording and graph findings, so category totals must not be added to obtain unique records. Wording comprises **19 clear-correction records, 289 recommended-polish records, and 29 optional-style records**. The {len(gi)} graph findings are organized into {len(g)} groups below.','', 'The main graph problem is that definitions or supplied conclusions resolve the question before students examine the figure. A second group has genuine graph tasks but only one economically coherent answer. These are assessment-design findings, not assertions that the keyed economics is wrong.','', '## Scope, method and preservation','']
for k,s in methods.items():lines.append(s+'\n')
lines+=['The bank includes **1,267 canonical records shared with General Economics**. The only shared records flagged are **40032** and **PG1-SUP-L-001**. Neither appears in the 126-item General wording/graph cleanup or the 38-item construct-drift closure. Their residual choice-elimination problems are documented explicitly below; their approved economic constructs, difficulty and routing should remain intact.','', 'Normal economics terminology is retained. There is no blanket objection to marginal cost, elasticity, Nash equilibrium, opportunity cost, surplus, a vertical gap, or a triangle/rectangle when the geometry helps identify an economic quantity. Likewise, “chosen output” is not globally replaced: an arbitrary stated output need not be an optimum. No residual “ledger” or “local inference” wording was found in the unshared Micro text screen.','', f'Canonical source: `{source}`. SHA-256 before and after: `{baseline[source]}`. All **{len(baseline):,}** preexisting files recorded under `build/`, `faculty_exports/` and `tools/` matched their baseline hashes (excluding Python cache files). Questions, answer keys/hashes, metadata, routing, graph assets, prior reports, exports and tests remain unchanged. No exporter regeneration or test-suite run was performed for this read-only review.','', 'The [machine-readable worklist](microeconomics_wording_graph_audit_20261003.json) contains exact current stems, all four choices, current keys, feedback and finding links for every affected record. The [coverage manifest](microeconomics_wording_graph_audit_20261003_coverage.json) lists all 6,301 screened IDs and all referenced assets with hashes. Current text in this report is evidence, not a proposed replacement.','', '## Wording findings','', 'Each group identifies one specific edit direction. IDs are explicit so repeated templates do not silently broaden the eventual cleanup. Shared General records are excluded from stylistic findings.','']
