lines += ['## Graph-assessment findings','', 'For each finding, both the image and its equivalent accessibility description were hidden. “Directly optional graph” means the textual task/theory already supplies the answer; “Graph-choice shortcut” means the alternatives bypass an otherwise legitimate graph task. Current stems and keys are listed for every affected ID; full alternatives are in the companion worklist.','', '**Required standard for any later repair:** at least two choices must remain economically plausible before the graph is seen. At least one distractor should, where practical, combine a real reading with an incorrect economic interpretation. The original concept must still distinguish the answers.','', '**Two acceptance tests:** Could coordinates alone answer the repaired question while the economics is ignored? **Required: NO.** Could economic theory alone identify the key with both image and accessibility description hidden? **Required: NO.** These are design requirements for the proposed directions below; final replacements have not been drafted or validated.','']
