lines += ['', '## Incidental correctness findings','', 'No separate high-priority economic or answer-key error was confirmed incidentally. The incomplete quotations, missing graphical references and unspecified threat are recorded as clear wording corrections. This review did not re-audit keys, difficulty, routing or economic-validity adjudications; the absence of an incidental finding is not a fresh certification of those dimensions.','', '## Final recommendation','', '| Category | Groups | Distinct records | Recommendation |','|---|---:|---:|---|','| A. Clear wording corrections | 7 | 19 | Repair incomplete stems, missing references, agreement and ambiguous threat/equilibrium wording first. |','| B. Recommended prose polish | 21 | 289 | Rewrite only the identified phrase or template; keep economics and assumptions. |','| C. Optional style changes | 4 | 29 | Defer until substantive work is complete; these are instructor preferences. |',f'| D. Directly optional graphs | {sum(x["kind"]=="direct" for x in g)} | {metrics["directly_optional_graph_questions"]} | Make a missing plotted fact necessary while retaining the original economic inference. |',f'| E. Graph-choice shortcuts | {sum(x["kind"]=="shortcut" for x in g)} | {metrics["graph_choice_shortcut_questions"]} | Strengthen alternatives so at least two survive theory alone. |','', 'Recommended order: **A → D and E together by overlapping record → B → C**. For each graph item, write down the original construct before editing, obtain the necessary evidence from the existing figure, and check the two acceptance tests. Coordinate overlapping prose and graph findings in one revision. Preserve the two shared General items’ earlier approved constructs and levels.','', '**No questions or exports were changed. This report supplies directions only; a later cleanup would need its own item-level validation and normal repository checks.**','']
